    "id": "71c1fc5e20aaa7114774",
    "source": "tab does too. Before anything is copied, the review says what each pick brings along: WorldForge brings the people, places, factions and lore it describes, and the hand-built monsters and items your prep uses are copied into that table&apos;s Bestiary and Homebrew, so its fights and World entries work there as they did here. Copies are copies: the workshop keeps its version, the campaign owns its own from then on, and name collisions get numbered instead of overwritten. The Share tool exports the whole workshop as a bundle file another server can import, and can compile a draft world pack from it.",
